WEBVTT

00:00.360 --> 00:03.870
In this video I want to do a
bunch of examples of factoring

00:03.870 --> 00:06.590
a second degree polynomial,
which is

00:06.590 --> 00:08.870
often called a quadratic.

00:08.870 --> 00:12.650
Sometimes a quadratic
polynomial, or just a

00:12.650 --> 00:15.850
quadratic itself, or quadratic
expression, but all it means

00:15.850 --> 00:18.300
is a second degree polynomial.

00:18.300 --> 00:22.440
So something that's going to
have a variable raised to the

00:22.440 --> 00:23.080
second power.

00:23.080 --> 00:26.460
In this case, in all of the
examples we'll do, it'll be x.

00:26.460 --> 00:30.740
So let's say I have the
quadratic expression, x

00:30.740 --> 00:35.280
squared plus 10x, plus 9.

00:35.280 --> 00:39.870
And I want to factor it into the
product of two binomials.

00:39.870 --> 00:41.520
How do we do that?

00:41.520 --> 00:44.440
Well, let's just think about
what happens if we were to

00:44.440 --> 00:51.690
take x plus a, and multiply
that by x plus b.

00:51.690 --> 00:55.050
If we were to multiply these
two things, what happens?

00:55.050 --> 00:57.090
Well, we have a little bit
of experience doing this.

00:57.090 --> 01:03.170
This will be x times x, which is
x squared, plus x times b,

01:03.170 --> 01:12.690
which is bx, plus a times x,
plus a times b-- plus ab.

01:12.690 --> 01:15.800
Or if we want to add these two
in the middle right here,

01:15.800 --> 01:18.890
because they're both
coefficients of x.

01:18.890 --> 01:22.102
We could right this as x squared
plus-- I can write it

01:22.102 --> 01:29.700
as b plus a, or a plus
b, x, plus ab.

01:29.700 --> 01:34.390
So in general, if we assume that
this is the product of

01:34.390 --> 01:40.765
two binomials, we see that this
middle coefficient on the

01:40.765 --> 01:43.250
x term, or you could say the
first degree coefficient

01:43.250 --> 01:49.040
there, that's going to be
the sum of our a and b.

01:49.040 --> 01:51.360
And then the constant term is
going to be the product

01:51.360 --> 01:52.520
of our a and b.

01:52.520 --> 01:57.290
Notice, this would map
to this, and this

01:57.290 --> 01:58.790
would map to this.

01:58.790 --> 02:02.600
And, of course, this is the
same thing as this.

02:02.600 --> 02:05.590
So can we somehow pattern
match this to that?

02:05.590 --> 02:14.060
Is there some a and b where
a plus b is equal to 10?

02:14.060 --> 02:22.070
And a times b is equal to 9?

02:22.070 --> 02:23.850
Well, let's just think about
it a little bit.

02:23.850 --> 02:25.470
What are the factors of 9?

02:25.470 --> 02:27.770
What are the things that a
and b could be equal to?

02:27.770 --> 02:29.170
And we're assuming that
everything is an integer.

02:29.170 --> 02:32.350
And normally when we're
factoring, especially when

02:32.350 --> 02:33.950
we're beginning to factor,
we're dealing

02:33.950 --> 02:35.580
with integer numbers.

02:35.580 --> 02:37.080
So what are the factors of 9?

02:37.080 --> 02:40.730
They're 1, 3, and 9.

02:40.730 --> 02:45.000
So this could be a 3 and a 3,
or it could be a 1 and a 9.

02:45.000 --> 02:48.630
Now, if it's a 3 and a 3, then
you'll have 3 plus 3-- that

02:48.630 --> 02:49.840
doesn't equal 10.

02:49.840 --> 02:53.760
But if it's a 1 and a
9, 1 times 9 is 9.

02:53.760 --> 02:56.670
1 plus 9 is 10.

02:56.670 --> 02:57.570
So it does work.

02:57.570 --> 03:04.190
So a could be equal to 1, and
b could be equal to 9.

03:04.190 --> 03:08.920
So we could factor this
as being x plus 1,

03:08.920 --> 03:12.970
times x plus 9.

03:12.970 --> 03:15.850
And if you multiply these two
out, using the skills we

03:15.850 --> 03:18.970
developed in the last few
videos, you'll see that it is

03:18.970 --> 03:22.880
indeed x squared plus
10x, plus 9.

03:22.880 --> 03:25.150
So when you see something like
this, when the coefficient on

03:25.150 --> 03:28.070
the x squared term, or the
leading coefficient on this

03:28.070 --> 03:31.650
quadratic is a 1, you can just
say, all right, what two

03:31.650 --> 03:34.530
numbers add up to this
coefficient right here?

03:37.720 --> 03:39.870
And those same two numbers, when
you take their product,

03:39.870 --> 03:41.660
have to be equal to 9.

03:41.660 --> 03:43.510
And of course, this has to
be in standard form.

03:43.510 --> 03:46.000
Or if it's not in standard form,
you should put it in

03:46.000 --> 03:48.500
that form, so that you can
always say, OK, whatever's on

03:48.500 --> 03:51.530
the first degree coefficient,
my a and b

03:51.530 --> 03:52.300
have to add to that.

03:52.300 --> 03:55.890
Whatever's my constant term, my
a times b, the product has

03:55.890 --> 03:56.370
to be that.

03:56.370 --> 03:58.150
Let's do several
more examples.

03:58.150 --> 04:00.510
I think the more examples
we do the more

04:00.510 --> 04:02.630
sense this'll make.

04:02.630 --> 04:08.700
Let's say we had x squared
plus 10x, plus-- well, I

04:08.700 --> 04:11.100
already did 10x, let's do a
different number-- x squared

04:11.100 --> 04:15.366
plus 15x, plus 50.

04:15.366 --> 04:17.470
And we want to factor this.

04:17.470 --> 04:20.339
Well, same drill.

04:20.339 --> 04:22.600
We have an x squared term.

04:22.600 --> 04:25.130
We have a first degree term.

04:25.130 --> 04:27.960
This right here should be
the sum of two numbers.

04:27.960 --> 04:30.620
And then this term, the constant
term right here,

04:30.620 --> 04:32.870
should be the product
of two numbers.

04:32.870 --> 04:35.640
So we need to think of two
numbers that, when I multiply

04:35.640 --> 04:39.220
them I get 50, and when
I add them, I get 15.

04:39.220 --> 04:41.910
And this is going to be a bit of
an art that you're going to

04:41.910 --> 04:44.530
develop, but the more practice
you do, you're going to see

04:44.530 --> 04:45.730
that it'll start to
come naturally.

04:45.730 --> 04:47.330
So what could a and b be?

04:47.330 --> 04:48.975
Let's think about the
factors of 50.

04:48.975 --> 04:52.230
It could be 1 times 50.

04:52.230 --> 04:55.072
2 times 25.

04:55.072 --> 04:57.520
Let's see, 4 doesn't
go into 50.

04:57.520 --> 05:02.450
It could be 5 times 10.

05:02.450 --> 05:03.580
I think that's all of them.

05:03.580 --> 05:05.920
Let's try out these numbers,
and see if any of

05:05.920 --> 05:07.310
these add up to 15.

05:07.310 --> 05:12.630
So 1 plus 50 does not
add up to 15.

05:12.630 --> 05:16.160
2 plus 25 does not
add up to 15.

05:16.160 --> 05:19.260
But 5 plus 10 does
add up to 15.

05:19.260 --> 05:24.280
So this could be 5 plus 10, and
this could be 5 times 10.

05:24.280 --> 05:28.760
So if we were to factor this,
this would be equal to x plus

05:28.760 --> 05:32.630
5, times x plus 10.

05:32.630 --> 05:33.840
And multiply it out.

05:33.840 --> 05:36.710
I encourage you to multiply this
out, and see that this is

05:36.710 --> 05:39.660
indeed x squared plus
15x, plus 10.

05:39.660 --> 05:43.320
In fact, let's do it. x
times x, x squared. x

05:43.320 --> 05:45.800
times 10, plus 10x.

05:45.800 --> 05:48.600
5 times x, plus 5x.

05:48.600 --> 05:51.620
5 times 10, plus 50.

05:51.620 --> 05:55.220
Notice, the 5 times
10 gave us the 50.

05:55.220 --> 06:00.890
The 5x plus the 10x is giving
us the 15x in between.

06:00.890 --> 06:06.560
So it's x squared plus
15x, plus 50.

06:06.560 --> 06:09.440
Let's up the stakes a little
bit, introduce some negative

06:09.440 --> 06:11.040
signs in here.

06:11.040 --> 06:18.890
Let's say I had x squared
minus 11x, plus 24.

06:18.890 --> 06:21.610
Now, it's the exact
same principle.

06:21.610 --> 06:24.580
I need to think of two numbers,
that when I add them,

06:24.580 --> 06:26.570
need to be equal
to negative 11.

06:26.570 --> 06:30.150
a plus b need to be equal
to negative 11.

06:30.150 --> 06:37.900
And a times b need to
be equal to 24.

06:37.900 --> 06:41.290
Now, there's something for
you to think about.

06:41.290 --> 06:43.960
When I multiply both of these
numbers, I'm getting a

06:43.960 --> 06:45.080
positive number.

06:45.080 --> 06:46.960
I'm getting a 24.

06:46.960 --> 06:50.260
That means that both of these
need to be positive, or both

06:50.260 --> 06:51.380
of these need to be negative.

06:51.380 --> 06:55.050
That's the only way I'm going to
get a positive number here.

06:55.050 --> 06:58.290
Now, if when I add them, I get
a negative number, if these

06:58.290 --> 07:00.720
were positive, there's no way I
can add two positive numbers

07:00.720 --> 07:03.280
and get a negative number, so
the fact that their sum is

07:03.280 --> 07:05.750
negative, and the fact that
their product is positive,

07:05.750 --> 07:10.420
tells me that both a
and b are negative.

07:10.420 --> 07:13.200
a and b have to be negative.

07:13.200 --> 07:15.730
Remember, one can't be negative
and the other one

07:15.730 --> 07:18.710
can't be positive, because the
product would be negative.

07:18.710 --> 07:22.687
And they both can't be positive,
because when you add

07:22.687 --> 07:24.520
them it would get you
a positive number.

07:24.520 --> 07:27.500
So let's just think about
what a and b can be.

07:27.500 --> 07:28.990
So two negative numbers.

07:28.990 --> 07:31.260
So let's think about
the factors of 24.

07:31.260 --> 07:33.140
And we'll kind of have to think
of the negative factors.

07:33.140 --> 07:44.670
But let me see, it could be 1
times 24, 2 times 11, 3 times

07:44.670 --> 07:48.070
8, or 4 times 6.

07:48.070 --> 07:51.220
Now, which of these when I
multiply these-- well,

07:51.220 --> 07:54.380
obviously when I multiply
1 times 24, I get 24.

07:54.380 --> 07:58.910
When I get 2 times 11-- sorry,
this is 2 times 12.

07:58.910 --> 07:59.790
I get 24.

07:59.790 --> 08:03.090
So we know that all these,
the products are 24.

08:03.090 --> 08:07.470
But which two of these, which
two factors, when I add them,

08:07.470 --> 08:08.790
should I get 11?

08:08.790 --> 08:09.880
And then we could say,
let's take the

08:09.880 --> 08:11.450
negative of both of those.

08:11.450 --> 08:15.470
So when you look at these,
3 and 8 jump out.

08:15.470 --> 08:19.150
3 times 8 is equal to 24.

08:19.150 --> 08:22.810
3 plus 8 is equal to 11.

08:22.810 --> 08:24.680
But that doesn't quite
work out, right?

08:24.680 --> 08:26.510
Because we have a negative
11 here.

08:26.510 --> 08:29.690
But what if we did negative
3 and negative 8?

08:29.690 --> 08:37.789
Negative 3 times negative 8
is equal to positive 24.

08:37.789 --> 08:43.580
Negative 3 plus negative 8
is equal to negative 11.

08:43.580 --> 08:46.600
So negative 3 and
negative 8 work.

08:46.600 --> 08:53.840
So if we factor this, x squared
minus 11x, plus 24 is

08:53.840 --> 09:02.940
going to be equal to x minus
3, times x minus 8.

09:02.940 --> 09:06.270
Let's do another
one like that.

09:06.270 --> 09:08.330
Actually, let's mix it
up a little bit.

09:08.330 --> 09:19.810
Let's say I had x squared
plus 5x, minus 14.

09:19.810 --> 09:21.770
So here we have a different
situation.

09:21.770 --> 09:26.460
The product of my two numbers is
negative, right? a times b

09:26.460 --> 09:28.190
is equal to negative 14.

09:28.190 --> 09:29.920
My product is negative.

09:29.920 --> 09:32.930
That tells me that one of them
is positive, and one of them

09:32.930 --> 09:33.910
is negative.

09:33.910 --> 09:39.200
And when I add the two, a plus
b, it'd be equal to 5.

09:39.200 --> 09:41.360
So let's think about
the factors of 14.

09:41.360 --> 09:44.300
And what combinations of them,
when I add them, if one is

09:44.300 --> 09:46.560
positive and one is negative,
or I'm really kind of taking

09:46.560 --> 09:49.780
the difference of the
two, do I get 5?

09:49.780 --> 09:53.450
So if I take 1 and 14-- I'm just
going to try out things--

09:53.450 --> 10:01.820
1 and 14, negative 1 plus
14 is negative 13.

10:01.820 --> 10:04.260
Negative 1 plus 14 is 13.

10:04.260 --> 10:07.430
So let me write all of the
combinations that I could do.

10:07.430 --> 10:09.440
And eventually your brain
will just zone in on it.

10:09.440 --> 10:16.490
So you've got negative 1
plus 14 is equal to 13.

10:16.490 --> 10:20.460
And 1 plus negative 14 is
equal to negative 13.

10:20.460 --> 10:21.380
So those don't work.

10:21.380 --> 10:22.950
That doesn't equal 5.

10:22.950 --> 10:24.860
Now what about 2 and 7?

10:24.860 --> 10:29.600
If I do negative 2-- let me do
this in a different color-- if

10:29.600 --> 10:35.290
I do negative 2 plus 7,
that is equal to 5.

10:35.290 --> 10:35.750
We're done!

10:35.750 --> 10:36.670
That worked!

10:36.670 --> 10:39.440
I mean, we could have tried 2
plus negative 7, but that'd be

10:39.440 --> 10:41.070
equal to negative 5, so that
wouldn't have worked.

10:41.070 --> 10:42.960
But negative 2 plus 7 works.

10:42.960 --> 10:46.590
And negative 2 times
7 is negative 14.

10:46.590 --> 10:47.600
So there we have it.

10:47.600 --> 10:53.210
We know it's x minus
2, times x plus 7.

10:53.210 --> 10:54.330
That's pretty neat.

10:54.330 --> 10:56.950
Negative 2 times 7
is negative 14.

10:56.950 --> 11:00.880
Negative 2 plus 7
is positive 5.

11:03.760 --> 11:07.680
Let's do several more of these,
just to really get well

11:07.680 --> 11:09.520
honed this skill.

11:09.520 --> 11:16.360
So let's say we have x squared
minus x, minus 56.

11:16.360 --> 11:19.570
So the product of the two
numbers have to be minus 56,

11:19.570 --> 11:21.620
have to be negative 56.

11:21.620 --> 11:24.430
And their difference, because
one is going to be positive,

11:24.430 --> 11:26.280
and one is going to be
negative, right?

11:26.280 --> 11:28.350
Their difference has
to be negative 1.

11:28.350 --> 11:30.130
And the numbers that immediately
jump out in my

11:30.130 --> 11:31.900
brain-- and I don't know if they
jump out in your brain,

11:31.900 --> 11:33.740
we just learned this in
the times tables--

11:33.740 --> 11:36.480
56 is 8 times 7.

11:36.480 --> 11:37.480
I mean, there's other numbers.

11:37.480 --> 11:39.950
It's also 28 times 2.

11:39.950 --> 11:41.140
It's all sorts of things.

11:41.140 --> 11:44.300
But 8 times 7 really jumped
out into my brain, because

11:44.300 --> 11:45.470
they're very close
to each other.

11:45.470 --> 11:47.730
And we need numbers that are
very close to each other.

11:47.730 --> 11:50.430
And one of these has to be
positive, and one of these has

11:50.430 --> 11:51.810
to be negative.

11:51.810 --> 11:55.250
Now, the fact that when their
sum is negative, tells me that

11:55.250 --> 11:58.460
the larger of these two should
probably be negative.

11:58.460 --> 12:01.350
So if we take negative
8 times 7, that's

12:01.350 --> 12:03.320
equal to negative 56.

12:03.320 --> 12:08.470
And then if we take negative
8 plus 7, that is equal to

12:08.470 --> 12:12.100
negative 1, which is exactly the
coefficient right there.

12:12.100 --> 12:16.490
So when I factor this, this
is going to be x minus 8,

12:16.490 --> 12:18.690
times x plus 7.

12:18.690 --> 12:21.695
This is often one of the hardest
concepts people learn

12:21.695 --> 12:23.920
in algebra, because it
is a bit of an art.

12:23.920 --> 12:26.710
You have to look at all of the
factors here, play with the

12:26.710 --> 12:29.710
positive and negative signs,
see which of those factors

12:29.710 --> 12:31.900
when one is positive, one is
negative, add up to the

12:31.900 --> 12:33.590
coefficient on the x term.

12:33.590 --> 12:35.860
But as you do more and more
practice, you'll see that

12:35.860 --> 12:39.280
it'll become a bit
of second nature.

12:39.280 --> 12:42.350
Now let's step up the stakes
a little bit more.

12:42.350 --> 12:46.140
Let's say we had negative x
squared-- everything we've

12:46.140 --> 12:49.040
done so far had a positive
coefficient, a positive 1

12:49.040 --> 12:50.690
coefficient on the
x squared term.

12:50.690 --> 12:55.590
But let's say we had a
negative x squared

12:55.590 --> 12:59.440
minus 5x, plus 24.

12:59.440 --> 13:00.910
How do we do this?

13:00.910 --> 13:03.420
Well, the easiest way I can
think of doing it is factor

13:03.420 --> 13:05.670
out a negative 1, and then it
becomes just like the problems

13:05.670 --> 13:07.260
we've been doing before.

13:07.260 --> 13:11.660
So this is the same thing as
negative 1 times positive x

13:11.660 --> 13:15.990
squared, plus 5x, minus 24.

13:15.990 --> 13:16.300
Right?

13:16.300 --> 13:18.080
I just factored a
negative 1 out.

13:18.080 --> 13:20.180
You can multiply negative 1
times all of these, and you'll

13:20.180 --> 13:21.690
see it becomes this.

13:21.690 --> 13:23.555
Or you could factor the negative
1 out and divide all

13:23.555 --> 13:25.000
of these by negative 1.

13:25.000 --> 13:26.760
And you get that right there.

13:26.760 --> 13:29.360
Now, same game as before.

13:29.360 --> 13:33.510
I need two numbers, that when
I take their product I get

13:33.510 --> 13:34.690
negative 24.

13:34.690 --> 13:37.125
So one will be positive,
one will be negative.

13:41.550 --> 13:43.770
When I take their sum,
it's going to be 5.

13:43.770 --> 13:48.850
So let's think about
24 is 1 and 24.

13:48.850 --> 13:55.750
Let's see, if this is negative 1
and 24, it'd be positive 23,

13:55.750 --> 13:57.540
if it was the other way around,
it'd be negative 23.

13:57.540 --> 13:58.500
Doesn't work.

13:58.500 --> 14:01.210
What about 2 and 12?

14:01.210 --> 14:04.530
Well, if this is negative--
remember, one of these has to

14:04.530 --> 14:05.040
be negative.

14:05.040 --> 14:07.570
If the 2 is negative, their
sum would be 10.

14:07.570 --> 14:09.750
If the 12 is negative, their
sum would be negative 10.

14:09.750 --> 14:11.300
Still doesn't work.

14:11.300 --> 14:13.290
3 and 8.

14:13.290 --> 14:16.850
If the 3 is negative,
their sum will be 5.

14:16.850 --> 14:17.910
So it works!

14:17.910 --> 14:24.620
So if we pick negative 3 and
8, negative 3 and 8 work.

14:24.620 --> 14:26.630
Because negative
3 plus 8 is 5.

14:26.630 --> 14:29.510
Negative 3 times 8
is negative 24.

14:29.510 --> 14:31.640
So this is going to be equal
to-- can't forget that

14:31.640 --> 14:35.230
negative 1 out front, and then
we factor the inside.

14:35.230 --> 14:42.990
Negative 1 times x minus
3, times x plus 8.

14:42.990 --> 14:44.800
And if you really wanted to,
you could multiply the

14:44.800 --> 14:46.450
negative 1 times this,
you would get 3

14:46.450 --> 14:47.560
minus x if you did.

14:47.560 --> 14:48.810
Or you don't have to.

14:51.810 --> 14:53.220
Let's do one more of these.

14:53.220 --> 14:56.060
The more practice, the
better, I think.

14:56.060 --> 15:01.630
All right, let's say I had
negative x squared

15:01.630 --> 15:06.690
plus 18x, minus 72.

15:06.690 --> 15:09.320
So once again, I like to factor
out the negative 1.

15:09.320 --> 15:13.040
So this is equal to negative
1 times x squared,

15:13.040 --> 15:16.910
minus 18x, plus 72.

15:16.910 --> 15:19.650
Now we just have to think of
two numbers, that when I

15:19.650 --> 15:22.330
multiply them I get
positive 72.

15:22.330 --> 15:24.480
So they have to be
the same sign.

15:24.480 --> 15:26.930
And that makes it easier in our
head, at least in my head.

15:26.930 --> 15:29.260
When I multiply them,
I get positive 72.

15:29.260 --> 15:32.040
When I add them, I
get negative 18.

15:32.040 --> 15:34.410
So they're the same sign, and
their sum is a negative

15:34.410 --> 15:36.470
number, they both must
be negative.

15:41.470 --> 15:43.790
And we could go through all
of the factors of 72.

15:43.790 --> 15:48.510
But the one that springs up,
maybe you think of 8 times 9,

15:48.510 --> 15:53.270
but 8 times 9, or negative 8
minus 9, or negative 8 plus

15:53.270 --> 15:55.210
negative 9, doesn't work.

15:55.210 --> 15:58.060
That turns into 17.

15:58.060 --> 15:58.860
That was close.

15:58.860 --> 15:59.560
Let me show you that.

15:59.560 --> 16:04.400
Negative 9 plus negative 8, that
is equal to negative 17.

16:04.400 --> 16:06.140
Close, but no cigar.

16:06.140 --> 16:06.990
So what other ones are there?

16:06.990 --> 16:08.005
We have 6 and 12.

16:08.005 --> 16:09.705
That actually seems
pretty good.

16:09.705 --> 16:13.710
If we have negative 6 plus
negative 12, that is equal to

16:13.710 --> 16:15.360
negative 18.

16:15.360 --> 16:16.590
Notice, it's a bit of an art.

16:16.590 --> 16:18.810
You have to try the different
factors here.

16:18.810 --> 16:22.360
So this will become negative
1-- don't want to forget

16:22.360 --> 16:29.440
that-- times x minus 6,
times x minus 12.
